{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Actor Component Model.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Actor Component Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"actor component model actor component model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Actor Component Model.md","fileName":"Actor Component Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Actor Component Model","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-20 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C++ Game Engine Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Game Engine Architecture","Game Actor","Game Component","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Actor Component Model.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Actor Component Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"actor component model actor component model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Actor Component Model.md","fileName":"Actor Component Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Actor Component Model","heading":"Actor Component Model","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The actor-component model gives each [[Game Actor]] a small common identity and transform while attaching separate [[Game Component|components]] for capabilities such as movement, drawing, input, audio, or collision. Behavior is composed instead of being forced into a deep inheritance tree.\n\nA hybrid design can still subclass actors for game-specific coordination while reusing components across those subclasses. The model keeps orthogonal features independent and lets one actor own several cooperating behaviors.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Game Engine Architecture","Game Actor","Game Component","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Actor Component Model.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Actor Co